---
import LegalPage from '../../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import LegalOwner from '../../../components/legal/LegalOwner.astro';
import { BLINDNOTE_MIN_AGE, BLINDNOTE_OWNER, LEGAL_EMAIL } from '../../../lib/legal';
import { route } from '../../../i18n';
---
<LegalPage
  lang="en"
  routeKey="blindnoteTerms"
  title="BlindNote Terms of Use | Kuxar Studio"
  heading="BlindNote Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use of the BlindNote app: requirements, private use with Spotify, licence, ads, song catalogue and liability."
  updated="26 November 2026"
>
  <p>These terms govern the use of <strong>BlindNote</strong>, the Android music quiz where you pass the phone around in turns to guess the artist, title and year of the song playing in Spotify. They are the terms on which we offer it, and you can read them at any time on this page or from <strong>Settings &gt; Information</strong>. If you do not agree with them, do not use the app.</p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>BlindNote is free, funded by ads, with no purchases.</li>
    <li>It is for playing privately with your people. Do not use it to play music in bars, venues or public events: Spotify's terms do not allow it.</li>
    <li>BlindNote does not include any music. You need the Spotify app and must follow its terms.</li>
    <li>You must be at least {BLINDNOTE_MIN_AGE} years old.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. Who provides BlindNote</h2>
  <LegalOwner owner={BLINDNOTE_OWNER} lang="en" />

  <h2>2. Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Be at least {BLINDNOTE_MIN_AGE} years old.</li>
    <li>Have the Spotify app installed, with an account signed in and an internet connection. Spotify Premium is recommended: with a free account, Spotify may play its own ads and apply its limits during the game.</li>
    <li>Give BlindNote Android's notification access, which it uses only to see and control the music in Spotify. We explain this in the <a href={route('blindnotePrivacy', 'en')}>privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Private use and Spotify's terms</h2>
  <p>BlindNote does not include songs: the music plays in your Spotify app, with your account, and BlindNote is the referee. So when you play you must also follow <a href="https://www.spotify.com/ie/legal/end-user-agreement/" rel="noopener">Spotify's terms of use</a>, which only allow personal, non-commercial use.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>You may use BlindNote to play at home or with friends.</li>
    <li><strong>Do not</strong> use it to play music in bars, restaurants, shops, gyms, public events or for any commercial purpose, for example quizzes with an entry fee or prizes run by a business.</li>
    <li>If you do, you are responsible towards Spotify and towards the rights holders of the music.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>BlindNote is compatible with Spotify, but it is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by Spotify. Spotify may change its app at any time, and this may stop BlindNote from working fully or in part.</p>

  <h2>4. Licence</h2>
  <p>We grant you a personal, free, non-exclusive and non-transferable licence to use BlindNote on your devices for private, non-commercial purposes. You may not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>copy, modify, decompile or redistribute the app, except as permitted by law;</li>
    <li>remove or block the ads by modifying the app;</li>
    <li>use the app for unlawful purposes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The code, design, texts and the BlindNote brand belong to Kuxar Studio.</p>

  <h2>5. Ads</h2>
  <p>BlindNote is free because it shows Google AdMob ads, at most one full-screen ad before the result of each game. What is processed to show them and how to change your choice are explained in the <a href={route('blindnotePrivacy', 'en')}>privacy policy</a>. The ads are chosen by Google and the advertisers, not by us; if you tap one, the website or app it leads to has its own terms.</p>

  <h2>6. The song catalogue</h2>
  <p>Each theme includes a list of songs with their title, artist and year, which we use to recognise what is playing and to show the answer. The years come from open music databases and we have reviewed them, but there may be mistakes: if you spot one, write to us. Artist and song names belong to their owners; BlindNote does not include recordings, lyrics or cover art.</p>

  <h2>7. Availability and changes to the app</h2>
  <p>We work to make BlindNote run well, but there may be interruptions or errors, especially if Spotify or Android change. We update the app to fix errors, improve how it works, renew the themes or adapt it to changes in Spotify, Android or the law. If an update significantly changes how the game is played, we will explain it in the release notes on Google Play. If we ever stop offering BlindNote, we will announce it with reasonable notice.</p>

  <h2>8. Liability</h2>
  <p>We are liable for BlindNote in accordance with the law, and nothing in these terms limits the rights that consumer protection law gives you. What Spotify, Google or other third-party services do on their own is governed by their own terms. And if you use the app against these terms or Spotify's, for example in a public venue, you are responsible for the consequences.</p>

  <h2>9. Privacy</h2>
  <p>How we process your data is explained in the <a href={route('blindnotePrivacy', 'en')}>BlindNote privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>We will only change these terms for a valid reason, such as a change in the app, in the law or in the third-party services it depends on. We will update the date above and, if the change is significant, we will announce it with reasonable notice in the release notes on Google Play or in the app itself. If you do not agree, you can stop using BlindNote and uninstall it.</p>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by Spanish law. If you are a consumer, you may bring a claim before the courts of your place of residence and you keep the protection of the mandatory rules of your country of residence.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a></p>
  <p><small>Spotify is a trademark of Spotify AB. Google, Android and AdMob are trademarks of Google LLC.</small></p>
</LegalPage>
